{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/72540-tell-me-what-makes-you-love-hunter-the-vigil","id":72540,"title":"Tell me what makes you love Hunter: The Vigil","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-15T03:35:18-08:00","id":72540,"title":"Tell me what makes you love Hunter: The Vigil","content":"So recently (relatively speaking) I was directed through the M:tAw forum to Dave Brookshaw's Broken Diamond AP, and went on from there to read his Soul Cage AP and now his third M:tAw AP. Before reading these, I had a cursory interest in Mage, but it didn't really grip me until reading these APs made it come alive.<br /> <br /> So now I'm looking into some of the other lines, and hoping the fans of those lines can open my eyes to their wonders, too.<br /> <br /> What do you love about Hunter: the Vigil? Tell me about it! A character you love, or one of those perfect roleplaying moments you've had. A post you read that perfectly encapsulated everything you felt about the game. An AP that captured your imagination. Anything!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T06:44:24-08:00","id":72586,"title":"","content":"I love it because its about not knowing. What if any supernatural senses and knowledge you have are limited and skewed. Is that pale guy running the local drug gang a Vampire or Changeling? What the hell is a Changeling? As humans you also can't just go off the grid and abandon your lives as easily as you can in Changeling, Vampire, Werewolf etc. If you can't live a normal life, you can't just wander into the forest and live on deer or mind meld someone in letting you stay in their apartment, you've got bills to pay and family that the darkness can retaliate against. So its a game where there are consequences to your mortal life for the actions you take against the supernatural and also to your psyche. Its also a wonderful vessel for fan service: love Superantural or the X-Files? This is your game. Complete with mechanics for making your own monsters, fluff that gives you carte blanche to deviate from the established lore of World of Darkness as you see fit and the ability to progress from season 1 Sam and Dean of Supernatural (two badass guys who are just humans with a lot of knowledge against the nightmares of the world) to being an actual, card carrying member of the Men in Black with monster hunting gizmos that level the playing field a little bit or a flaming sword wielding Paladin among other possibilities. It puts the mystery back into World of Darkness because if you tell the story right, player knowledge of all the various game lines just isn't going to help when your characters have no reason to know about or be told what the difference is between a Changeling contract and a Mage rote. All they see is a quirky fellow warping reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T07:57:36-08:00","id":72629,"title":"","content":"I love it because it involves normal, plain-as-dirt humans taking the fight to the things that go bump in the night and would treat them as inconsequential at best. The game is a statement that no, humans aren't going to be cattle - not all of them. From the ignorant, frightened rag-tag cell hunting down something they don't understand, to a well-equipped team of Malleus Maleficarum inquisitors torching an entire coterie of vampires, they put the fear back in the monsters. The hunters are the ultimate underdogs of the World of Darkness, and I do love underdog stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T15:58:35-08:00","id":72856,"title":"","content":"I love it because I can play a human. That hunts monsters. Alone, or with a group. Vastly underpowered. Unbeatable odds. Yet...in any given circumstance, the human--despite the odds--can WIN. Hunter the Vigil is my favorite NWOD gameline, as Hunter the Reckoning is my favorite CWOD. What can I say? It kicks ass to play a hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T17:33:47-08:00","id":72897,"title":"","content":"The World of Darkness is, for me, a setting about horror and mystery. Some of that is lessened when every character starts off a part of it. Hunters are normal people; getting to slowly pull back the curtain has a lot more impact if you aren't already a piece of the puzzle. Monsters get to be monsters. Nobody knows anything (and if they do, they're either wrong or halfway to being a monster themselves). Moral slippage. Conspiracy. A very real chance of death and insanity. It's a slightly pulpier, modern-day Call of Cthulhu, with the freedom to use any monster I like. I love it for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T19:01:48-08:00","id":73496,"title":"","content":"I like the mystery. There is a lot more unknown in this game than in the other lines. It's more about investigation and less about social intrigue. The hunter organisations are less focused on each other. They might hunt together once in a while and split up after that. There might be one organisation in a city, or five or none at all. It doesn't really matter much. It's very flexible that way.<br /> <br /> It also has one the best books in the nwod line: Slasher. And the recognition guide is awesome too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1873,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","user":"Jan Paparazzi","date":". 02-16-2014, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T21:25:25-08:00","id":73542,"title":"","content":"The fact that Hunter allows you to upend every paradigm about horror and urban fantasy if you want. You can have a traditional-style story about the darkness lurking behind the world centered around a greater conspiracy, or you can have a black comedy pulp story where the vampires are running the local petting zoo to suck young children half-dry. You can be Dr. Van Helsing, Agent Mulder, any number of pop culture monster hunters and truth seekers, or create your own new hunter who is something unique in their style and drive. You can be the hero or the villain, both if you play it right (or wrong). The monsters are yours to make and decide what they are, from the vengeful ghost and the self-loathing Frankenstein's monster, to the cyborg-clone hitmen under the control of a dark corporate entity, up to normal criminals who are just making your life hell. It's the sheer number of stories you can get out of it, and that's why I love Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T05:27:51-08:00","id":73667,"title":"","content":"Well, there are many many aspects that made me love HtV, but what really sold me to this book is the little fiction before Long Night section. It really did give a vibe of actual, everybody, people, with little or no power standing up against the powerful supernatural.<br /> <br /> I'm not even christian either, but the writing was thematically so good to describe the Hunters in the WoD in just a page.<br /> <br /> And I agree with Jan. Slasher is just too good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T10:07:33-08:00","id":73776,"title":"","content":"To me, Hunter is the Mage game I wanted.<br /> <br /> The PCs are normal humans. There are many diverse organisations with different attitudes, levels of mundane power and levels of supernatural power. There are many different kinds of magic which can do different things and work in different ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't have anything against games of ordinary humans fighting monsters, but I'm more interested in games where ordinary humans interact wit the supernatural world. Bargain with it, peruse esoteric philosophies to find spiritual fulfilment / enlightenment, or just check it out. Hunter is the game for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T12:41:46-08:00","id":73836,"title":"","content":"Hey, if you want a Mage game that is like Hunter, I might suggest picking up Unisystem's Witchcraft. The setup is nearly the same: Mage organisations only working together for hunting monsters, powers to make all the monsters you want, additional books for more vampire (Mystery codex) and werewolf (Abomination codex) powers and the core is free because it sold like $#!T.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}